l notice read the driver's two texts (all read_at null, and trip_record.in_app_calls empty), which is why an in-app message was not a reasonable way to reach you; but an unread message does not defeat a fee the driver otherwise earned, and the chat impairment goes to weight, not to the outcome. To the driver: your POL-NS-01 showing is accepted in full, and because no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, POL-NS-07 gives you compensation of 80 percent of the SGD 6.00 fee — SGD 4.80 — with the rider's charge standing unchanged. The anti-farming check does not bite, and both limbs are required: no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/168 is 0.006 (below 0.08). Two artifacts are impaired at schema level and I name them as POL-GEN-02(3) requires: the chat log EV-CHAT-00202 at weight 0.85 (UNREAD_MESSAGE) and the driver profile EV-DPROF-00202 at weight 0.9 (SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH); neither carries the deciding fact, both are down-weighted in confidence only, and the EUR finding survives because the arrival, dwell and termination rest on the GPS trace and trip record at weight 1.0. The confidence is set by the lowest-weighted artifact that carries part of the decision, the driver profile at 0.9, which is above the 0.70 floor. Some of the driver's specific submissions were discarded by the referee for failing to disclose the impairment of artifacts they cited; that discarding does not change this outcome, which follows from the policy and the record. No clause produces a referral here: the false-arrival referral in POL-NS-05(ii) is not reached (qualifying in-geofence fixes exist), and no driver-conduct or billing-integrity referral fires."
